<title>PHILIPPINES: JG Summit buys back 4.55 mln shares.</title>
<headline>JG Summit buys back 4.55 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>JG Summit Holdings Inc, the diversified holding company of Filipino-Chinese tycoon John Gokongwei, said on Tuesday it purchased 4.55 million of its own class B common shares.</p>
<p>JG Summit president James Go told the Securities and Exchange Commission that 1.35 million shares were bought on September 27 and 3.2 million shares on September 30.</p>
<p>JG Summit officials said the shares were bought at the &quot;prevailing market price.&quot; They declined to give reasons for the buyback.</p>
<p>JG Summit closed at 8.60 pesos a share on September 27, at 8.30 pesos on September 30 and at 8.50 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418936 fax 8176267</p>
